# Answer key for the "public-permits" gold dataset (Postgres) — HUMAN-MAINTAINED.
# Wave B1.b of Milestone 1.23 (F1.23.4): statistical-power wave.
# Story: municipal permitting platform after a four-district register consolidation —
# FKs re-added NOT VALID, portal submissions landing without constraints, 2005 register still read.
# See ./README.md for the planted-defect table.
#
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"permits","entity":"authorities","field":"website_url","severity":"medium","note":"planted: website_url is null for 15% (63/420) of authorities — the smaller district teams have no public page, so the statutory \"how to appeal\" link cannot be generated for their decisions."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"permits","entity":"authorities","field":"website_url","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 28 website_url values are bare domains with no scheme (\"planning.eastdistrict.gov\") — they fail the url format and render as dead links on the decision notice."}
{"dimension":"consistency","namespace":"permits","entity":"authorities","field":"region_cd","severity":"low","note":"planted: region_cd stored as NW / nw / Nw / SE / se ... — 28 raw values collapse to 22 normalized, so regional caseload statistics split the same region across spellings."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"permits","entity":"authorities","field":"authority_cd","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 8 duplicate authority codes on the declared UNIQUE key — two districts used the same short code for their planning and building-control teams, and consolidation kept both rows."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"permits","entity":"applicants","field":"contact_email","severity":"medium","note":"planted: contact_email is null for 14% (89600/640000) of applicants — counter and postal applications capture no address, so those applicants never receive an electronic decision notice."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"permits","entity":"applicants","field":"contact_email","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 4800 contact_email values are malformed (spaces, missing domain) — counter staff transcribe them from paper forms into an unvalidated field."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"permits","entity":"applicants","field":"mobile_number","severity":"medium","note":"planted: mobile_number is null for 19% (121600/640000) of applicants — no channel captures it consistently, so inspection-appointment SMS reaches four applicants in five at best."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"permits","entity":"applicants","field":"mobile_number","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 3100 mobile_number values are free text (\"home only\", \"call agent\") — they fail the phone format."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"permits","entity":"applicants","field":"national_ref","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 240 duplicate national_ref values on the declared UNIQUE key — the same person registered in two districts before consolidation, and the merge kept both identities."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"permits","entity":"applications","field":"use_class_cd","severity":"medium","note":"planted: use_class_cd is null on 12% (288000/2400000) of applications — the portal made it optional for householder work, so land-use statistics reported to central government exclude an eighth of the caseload."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"permits","entity":"applications","field":"decision_cd","severity":"medium","note":"planted: decision_cd is null on 16% (384000/2400000) of applications — undecided cases and cases decided in the pre-consolidation systems look identical, so the statutory 8-week performance figure is computed over the wrong denominator."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"permits","entity":"permits","field":"permit_uuid","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 9400 permit_uuid values are the district's old alphanumeric reference rather than a UUID — they fail the uuid format and break the national register submission."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"permits","entity":"permits","field":"conditions_text","severity":"medium","note":"planted: conditions_text is null on 40% (720000/1800000) of permits — unconditional permits legitimately have none, but so do the 40000 conditional permits whose conditions live only in the scanned PDF, and enforcement cannot tell them apart."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"permits","entity":"permits","field":"revoked_on","severity":"medium","note":"planted: revoked_on carries a 2099-12-31 sentinel for \"not revoked\" — a future date in the column enforcement reads to decide whether a permit is still live."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"permits","entity":"permits","field":"permit_no","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 940 duplicate permit numbers on the declared UNIQUE key — each district numbered permits from 1 each year, so consolidation produced collisions the merge never resolved."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"permits","entity":"fees","field":"receipt_ref","severity":"low","note":"planted: receipt_ref is null on 7% (217000/3100000) of fee rows — waived and exempt fees have no receipt, and so do the card payments whose reference the gateway failed to return, so unreconciled income has nothing to match on."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"permits","entity":"v_permit_status","field":"permit_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the status view is specified as one row per permit, but permits amended more than once appear once per amendment — 6400 duplicate permit_id values, so \"live permits\" is over-reported."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"permits","entity":"v_permit_status","field":"last_event_at","severity":"low","note":"planted: last_event_at is null for 6% (108000/1800000) of permits — permits migrated from the district registers carry no event history, so \"nothing has happened recently\" and \"we never knew what happened\" render the same."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"permits","entity":"stg_portal_submissions","field":"application_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 38400 duplicate application_id values in the portal landing table — the submission service retries on gateway timeouts, and every retry lands a second copy."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"permits","entity":"stg_portal_submissions","field":"submitted_date","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 31000 submitted_date values arrive as DD/MM/YYYY from the legacy portal skin instead of ISO — they fail the date-string format."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"permits","entity":"stg_portal_submissions","field":"received_ts","severity":"medium","note":"planted: received_ts reaches 2087-01-01 — a client-side timestamp from browsers with a wrong system clock is trusted verbatim, and those submissions sort to the top of every queue."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"permits","entity":"stg_gis_parcels","field":"parcel_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 8400 duplicate parcel_id values in the GIS landing table — the cadastre extract overlaps district boundaries, so parcels on a boundary arrive twice."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"permits","entity":"stg_gis_parcels","field":"survey_date","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 12000 survey_date values are the string \"n/a\" for parcels never re-surveyed since digitisation — they fail the date-string format."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"permits","entity":"stg_gis_parcels","field":"area_sqm","severity":"low","note":"planted: area_sqm reaches -1 — self-intersecting polygons produce a negative signed area, which is written straight through and then summed into district land-use totals."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"permits","entity":"legacy_permits_2005","field":"permit_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 11400 duplicate permit_id values — the four district registers were unioned without re-keying, so ids collide across districts."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"permits","entity":"legacy_permits_2005","field":"issued_on","severity":"low","note":"planted: issued_on reaches back to 1899-12-30 — the spreadsheet epoch, written by the digitisation project wherever the paper record had no legible date."}
{"dimension":"timeliness","namespace":"permits","entity":"legacy_permits_2005","field":"recorded_at","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the newest recorded_at is 2023-03-31 (1230 days stale) — the 2005-era register was frozen at consolidation, but the public \"historic permits\" search still reads it, so the site presents a decade-old view as current."}
{"dimension":"consistency","namespace":"inspect","entity":"inspectors","field":"discipline_cd","severity":"low","note":"planted: discipline_cd stored as BUILDING / building / Building / DRAINAGE / drainage ... — 18 raw values collapse to 13 normalized, so workload by discipline is wrong."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"inspect","entity":"inspectors","field":"team_cd","severity":"medium","note":"planted: team_cd is null for 12% (168/1400) of inspectors — contractors engaged during the backlog recovery were never assigned to a team, so their inspections appear in no team's statistics."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"inspect","entity":"inspectors","field":"badge_no","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 34 duplicate badge numbers on the declared UNIQUE key — each district issued its own badge series, and consolidation merged them without re-issuing."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"inspect","entity":"inspection_types","field":"statutory_basis","severity":"medium","note":"planted: statutory_basis is null for 25% (21/84) of inspection types — discretionary inspection types have none, but so do four statutory ones whose reference was lost, and enforcement notices cite this column."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"inspect","entity":"inspections","field":"duration_minutes","severity":"low","note":"planted: duration_minutes reaches -15 — inspectors close a visit on the tablet before the arrival timestamp syncs, producing negative durations that pull the average visit length down."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"inspect","entity":"inspections","field":"outcome_cd","severity":"low","note":"planted: outcome_cd is null on 9% (432000/4800000) of inspections — visits abandoned because nobody was on site are saved with no outcome, so \"no access\" is invisible in the statistics."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"inspect","entity":"inspections","field":"start_at, end_at","severity":"low","note":"planted: the whole end_at range (2018-11-05 … 2025-10-14) precedes the whole start_at range (2019-01-07 … 2026-08-11) — the tablet app writes the two columns the wrong way round for one district's device fleet."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"inspect","entity":"violations","field":"remedy_notes","severity":"medium","note":"planted: remedy_notes is null on 15% (141000/940000) of violations — the required remedy is recorded on the paper notice for the districts that never adopted the tablet, so the follow-up cannot be automated."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"inspect","entity":"v_inspector_load","field":"inspector_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the load view is specified as one row per inspector, but inspectors holding two disciplines appear twice — 42 duplicate inspector_id values, so team capacity is over-stated."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"inspect","entity":"v_inspector_load","field":"utilisation_pct","severity":"medium","note":"planted: utilisation_pct maxes at 137.5 in a column named as a percentage — booked hours are divided by contracted hours that ignore overtime, so inspectors appear to work more than their capacity."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"inspect","entity":"stg_field_reports","field":"inspection_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 76800 duplicate inspection_id values in the tablet-sync landing table — offline devices re-upload their whole queue after every reconnect."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"inspect","entity":"stg_field_reports","field":"report_date","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 61000 report_date values are device-locale strings (\"11 Aug 2026\") rather than ISO — they fail the date-string format."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"inspect","entity":"stg_field_reports","field":"score","severity":"low","note":"planted: score uses -99 as the tablet app's \"not scored\" sentinel — a negative in a 0-100 score column, which every average silently absorbs."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"inspect","entity":"legacy_complaints","field":"complaint_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 5400 duplicate complaint_id values — the four district complaint logs were unioned without re-keying."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"inspect","entity":"legacy_complaints","field":"received_on","severity":"low","note":"planted: received_on reaches back to 1801-01-01 — the district system's minimum date, written wherever the complaint pre-dated digitisation, so \"oldest unresolved complaint\" is meaningless."}
{"dimension":"timeliness","namespace":"inspect","entity":"legacy_complaints","field":"logged_at","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the newest logged_at is 2023-02-28 (1261 days stale) — the pre-consolidation complaints line was closed, but the annual enforcement return still counts rows from this table."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"permits","entity":"applications","field":"applicant_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 18400 applications reference an applicant_id with no applicants row — subject-access erasure requests delete the person and leave the case file."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"permits","entity":"applications","field":"authority_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 2400 applications name an authority that was dissolved in the consolidation and deleted rather than end-dated."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"permits","entity":"permits","field":"application_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 9400 permits have no parent application — permits migrated from the district registers arrived without their case file."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"permits","entity":"fees","field":"application_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 31000 fee rows reference a deleted application, so that income cannot be attributed to any case."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"inspect","entity":"inspections","field":"permit_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 84000 inspections reference a permit that does not exist — the cross-schema FK was left NOT VALID after the register merge."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"inspect","entity":"inspections","field":"inspector_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 12400 inspections reference an inspector who was hard-deleted when their contract ended, so the visit has no accountable officer."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"inspect","entity":"inspections","field":"inspection_type_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 1800 inspections use a type code retired and deleted rather than end-dated, so they fall out of every type-based report."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"inspect","entity":"violations","field":"inspection_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 6400 violations have no parent inspection — re-scheduled visits are deleted and re-created, orphaning the breaches already recorded."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"permits","entity":"v_permit_status","field":"permit_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the status view carries 4100 permit_id values with no permit row — it reads the landing table, which still holds permits withdrawn from the core register."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"permits","entity":"stg_portal_submissions","field":"application_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 26000 portal rows reference applications that were withdrawn and deleted between submission and load."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"permits","entity":"legacy_permits_2005","field":"permit_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 640000 rows of the 2005 register have ids that match no current permit — the registers were never re-keyed, so the historic search returns records the current system cannot resolve."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"inspect","entity":"v_inspector_load","field":"inspector_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the load view carries 12 inspector_id values with no inspector row — contractors deleted at the end of their engagement still appear in the capacity figures."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"inspect","entity":"stg_field_reports","field":"inspection_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 48000 tablet reports reference inspections that were re-scheduled (deleted and re-created) while the device was offline."}
{"dimension":"accessibility","namespace":"permits","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the readiness role has no SELECT on permits.permits_pii_vault (applicant identity documents held under the data-protection impact assessment) — 1 of 10 tables locked, so the namespace aggregates to ONE medium (partial) finding."}
{"dimension":"accessibility","namespace":"inspect","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the readiness role has no SELECT on inspect.inspect_case_notes (enforcement case notes withheld pending prosecution) — 1 of 8 tables locked, so the namespace aggregates to ONE medium (partial) finding."}
